        "unit": "V",
        "source": {
          "datasheet": {
            "doc": "2N7000/D Rev. 5",
            "at": "Figure 2 at 25 C, through (4.0 V, 0.20 A) and (5.0 V, 0.36 A), rounded to 1.08 V, inside ON CHARACTERISTICS VGS(th) of 0.8 V to 3.0 V at ID = 1.0 mA. A 3.3 V gate gives 0.115 A here, where Figure 2 reads about 0.07 A. The model conducts from 1.08 V. Figure 2's typical curve starts near 2.5 V, and at a 2.5 V gate the model gives about 0.047 A, where a typical part passes almost nothing",
